CORE
main.py
--unwind 18
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.\d+\] .* Python assertion: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
The solver's parse axioms exclude inputs whose value overflows the result
type, so parsing straight into 64 bits dropped every word starting with a
digit >= 8 and proved `w[0] != 'f'` (a false proof). The parse is now 128
bits wide; the value then wraps into the default 64-bit int model like
other symbolic arithmetic.
